@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-schedule1`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-definitions`

-- The Interpretation Act 1978 (1978 c. 30): references to EU instruments and to the EEA agreement.
-- Section 20(2A) to (6), section 20A, and the carve-out in section 22(1) that cuts those provisions down.
--
-- Source: the converter-made plain-text rendering in ../../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1978-30.txt, not the official text (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
--
-- Dates the text refers to without giving ("IP completion day", the day section 20A came into force) are INPUTS (fork F13): the caller says what they are.
-- "IP completion day" is a moment, and an Act is passed on a day, so an Act passed on that day is read as passed on it ("on or after"); the Act does not
-- say how a moment within the day is to be compared, and this module does not try (see NOTES.md, "What the text does not answer").
-- Terms that other Acts define (relevant separation agreement law, section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018) are asked as booleans.

§ `Nouns of this module`

DECLARE `Provision about references to EU instruments` IS ONE OF
    `section 20(2A)`
    `section 20(3)`
    `section 20(4)`
    `section 20(5)`
    `section 20(6)`
    `section 20A`

DECLARE `EU legislation that section 20(3) names` IS ONE OF
    `an EU regulation`
    `an EU decision`
    `EU tertiary legislation`
    `a provision of the EEA agreement`
    `something else`

DECLARE `How a reference is read` IS ONE OF
    `as it so has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018`
    `as it so has effect, including as it has effect from time to time`
    `as it forms part of domestic law by virtue of section 3 of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 or section 1 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020`
    `as so amended, extended or applied`
    `no reading is given by this provision`

DECLARE `Thing that section 20(6) counts as a treaty` IS ONE OF
    `a treaty`
    `an international agreement`
    `a protocol to a treaty or international agreement`
    `an annex to a treaty or international agreement`
    `something else`

§ `Named refusals of this module`

-- A refusal is an expression at any type; each name is its message.

-- src:93 | (4) Subsection (3) does not determine any question as to whether the reference is to be read as a reference to the EU regulation, EU decision, EU tertiary legislation or provision of the EEA agreement as modified by domestic law (and, accordingly, is without prejudice to subsection (2)).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(4) (src:93): subsection (3) does not determine whether the reference is to the document as modified by domestic law, and is without prejudice to subsection (2)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 20(4) leaves open whether the reference is to the document as modified by domestic law, and the sources do not answer it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 20(4) leaves open whether the reference is to the document as modified by domestic law, and the sources do not answer it"

-- src:93 | (4) Subsection (3) does not determine any question as to whether the reference is to be read as a reference to the EU regulation, EU decision, EU tertiary legislation or provision of the EEA agreement as modified by domestic law (and, accordingly, is without prejudice to subsection (2)).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(4) (src:93): the subsection speaks of a reference to which subsection (3) applies
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 20(4) says nothing about a reference to which subsection (3) does not apply` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 20(4) says nothing about a reference to which subsection (3) does not apply"

-- src:94 | (5) Any expression in subsections (2A) to (4) which is defined in the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 has the same meaning in the subsection concerned as in that Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(5) (src:94): the meaning is that of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018, which is not among the sources
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 20(5) takes the meaning from the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018, which is not among the sources, and the caller has not given it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 20(5) takes the meaning from the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018, which is not among the sources, and the caller has not given it"

§ `Section 20(2A): the withdrawal agreement`

-- "(2A) Where (a) an Act passed on or after IP completion day refers to any treaty relating to the EU or any instrument or other document of an EU entity, and
-- (b) the treaty, instrument or document has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018, the reference, unless the contrary
-- intention appears and so far as required for the purposes of relevant separation agreement law, is a reference to the treaty, instrument or document as it so has
-- effect (including, so far as so required, as it has effect from time to time)."
-- src:88 | (2A) Where—
-- src:89 | (a) an Act passed on or after IP completion day refers to any treaty relating to the EU or any instrument or other document of an EU entity, and
-- src:90 | (b) the treaty, instrument or document has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 (general implementation of remainder of EU withdrawal agreement etc.),
-- src:91 | the reference, unless the contrary intention appears and so far as required for the purposes of relevant separation agreement law, is a reference to the treaty, instrument or document as it so has effect (including, so far as so required, as it has effect from time to time).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(2A) (src:88-91), with s 22(1) (src:103)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `IP completion day` IS A DATE
      `the Act refers to a treaty relating to the EU or to an instrument or other document of an EU entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the treaty, instrument or document has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reading it so is required for the purposes of relevant separation agreement law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reading it as it has effect from time to time is so required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How a reference is read`
`section 20(2A) — how the reference is read` day `IP completion day` `the Act refers to a treaty relating to the EU or to an instrument or other document of an EU entity` `the treaty, instrument or document has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018` `the contrary intention appears` `reading it so is required for the purposes of relevant separation agreement law` `reading it as it has effect from time to time is so required` MEANS
    IF   day AT LEAST `IP completion day`
         AND `the Act refers to a treaty relating to the EU or to an instrument or other document of an EU entity`
         AND `the treaty, instrument or document has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018`
         AND (NOT `the contrary intention appears`)
         AND `reading it so is required for the purposes of relevant separation agreement law`
    THEN IF   `reading it as it has effect from time to time is so required`
         THEN `as it so has effect, including as it has effect from time to time`
         ELSE `as it so has effect by virtue of section 7A or 7B of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018`
    ELSE `no reading is given by this provision`

§ `Section 20(3) and (4): EU regulations, decisions, tertiary legislation and the EEA agreement`

-- "(3) Subject to subsection (2A), where an Act passed on or after IP completion day refers to any EU regulation, EU decision, EU tertiary legislation or provision
-- of the EEA agreement, the reference, unless the contrary intention appears, is a reference to the [thing] as it forms part of domestic law by virtue of section 3 of the
-- European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 or section 1 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020."
-- "Subject to subsection (2A)": where (2A) gives a reading, that reading stands.
-- src:92 | (3) Subject to subsection (2A), where an Act passed on or after IP completion day refers to any EU regulation, EU decision, EU tertiary legislation or provision of the EEA agreement, the reference, unless the contrary intention appears, is a reference to the EU regulation, EU decision, EU tertiary legislation or provision of the EEA agreement as it forms part of domestic law by virtue of section 3 of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 or section 1 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(3) (src:92), with s 22(1) (src:103)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `IP completion day` IS A DATE
      what IS AN `EU legislation that section 20(3) names`
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reading that section 20(2A) gives` IS A `How a reference is read`
GIVETH A `How a reference is read`
`section 20(3) — how the reference is read` day `IP completion day` what `the contrary intention appears` `the reading that section 20(2A) gives` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the reading that section 20(2A) gives` EQUALS `no reading is given by this provision`)
    THEN `the reading that section 20(2A) gives`
    ELSE IF   day AT LEAST `IP completion day`
              AND (NOT (what EQUALS `something else`))
              AND (NOT `the contrary intention appears`)
         THEN `as it forms part of domestic law by virtue of section 3 of the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 or section 1 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020`
         ELSE `no reading is given by this provision`

-- "(4) Subsection (3) does not determine any question as to whether the reference is to be read as a reference to the EU regulation, EU decision, EU tertiary
-- legislation or provision of the EEA agreement as modified by domestic law (and, accordingly, is without prejudice to subsection (2))."
-- src:93 | (4) Subsection (3) does not determine any question as to whether the reference is to be read as a reference to the EU regulation, EU decision, EU tertiary legislation or provision of the EEA agreement as modified by domestic law (and, accordingly, is without prejudice to subsection (2)).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(4) (src:93)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 20(4) provides that subsection (3) determines whether the reference is read as a reference to the thing as modified by domestic law` MEANS FALSE

-- src:93 | (4) Subsection (3) does not determine any question as to whether the reference is to be read as a reference to the EU regulation, EU decision, EU tertiary legislation or provision of the EEA agreement as modified by domestic law (and, accordingly, is without prejudice to subsection (2)).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(4) (src:93)
GIVEN `section 20(3) applies to the reference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 20(4) — whether the reference is read as a reference to the thing as modified by domestic law` `section 20(3) applies to the reference` MEANS
    IF   `section 20(3) applies to the reference`
    THEN `section 20(4) leaves open whether the reference is to the document as modified by domestic law, and the sources do not answer it`
    ELSE `section 20(4) says nothing about a reference to which subsection (3) does not apply`

§ `Section 20(5) and (6): meanings`

-- "(5) Any expression in subsections (2A) to (4) which is defined in the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 has the same meaning in the subsection concerned as in that Act."
-- The meaning is that Act's, which is not among the sources: the caller gives it, and this function returns it.
-- src:94 | (5) Any expression in subsections (2A) to (4) which is defined in the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 has the same meaning in the subsection concerned as in that Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(5) (src:94)
GIVEN `the expression is defined in the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meaning it has in that Act` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`section 20(5) — the meaning of the expression in subsections (2A) to (4)` `the expression is defined in the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018` `the meaning it has in that Act` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the expression is defined in the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the meaning it has in that Act`
         WHEN JUST meaning THEN JUST meaning
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `section 20(5) takes the meaning from the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018, which is not among the sources, and the caller has not given it`

-- src:95 | (6) In this section, “treaty” includes any international agreement (and any protocol or annex to a treaty or international agreement).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(6) (src:95): "treaty" includes any international agreement (and any protocol or annex)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that section 20(6) counts as a treaty`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 20(6) counts the thing as a treaty` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `a treaty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an international agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a protocol to a treaty or international agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an annex to a treaty or international agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE

§ `Section 20A: references to certain EU instruments`

-- "Where an Act passed after the commencement of this section refers to a EU instrument that has been amended, extended or applied by another such instrument,
-- the reference, unless the contrary intention appears, is a reference to that instrument as so amended, extended or applied."
-- A section comes into force at the beginning of its day (s 4), so an Act passed on that day is passed after the commencement of the section (as fork F9).
-- src:96 | 20A References to certain EU instruments
-- src:97 | Where an Act passed after the commencement of this section refers to a EU instrument that has been amended, extended or applied by another such instrument, the reference, unless the contrary intention appears, is a reference to that instrument as so amended, extended or applied.
-- src:373 | “EU instrument” means any instrument issued by an EU institution other than any assimilated direct legislation.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20A (src:96-97), with Sch 1 "EU instrument" (src:373)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day section 20A came into force` IS A DATE
      `it is an instrument issued by an EU institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is assimilated direct legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been amended, extended or applied by another such instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How a reference is read`
`section 20A — how the reference is read` day `the day section 20A came into force` `it is an instrument issued by an EU institution` `it is assimilated direct legislation` `it has been amended, extended or applied by another such instrument` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF   day AT LEAST `the day section 20A came into force`
         AND `Schedule 1 counts the instrument as an EU instrument` `it is an instrument issued by an EU institution` `it is assimilated direct legislation`
         AND `it has been amended, extended or applied by another such instrument`
         AND (NOT `the contrary intention appears`)
    THEN `as so amended, extended or applied`
    ELSE `no reading is given by this provision`

§ `Section 22(1): the carve-out for section 20(2A) to (6) and section 20A`

-- "This Act applies to itself, to any Act passed after the commencement of this Act (subject, in the case of section 20(2A) to (6), to the provision made in section 20(2A) or (3)
-- and, in the case of section 20A, to the provision made in that section)". Part I of Schedule 2 lists neither, so for an Act passed before the commencement they do not apply (fork F15).
-- After the commencement, section 20(2A) to (6) reach only Acts passed on or after IP completion day, as (2A) and (3) say, and section 20A only Acts passed after its own
-- commencement (fork F26). The new provisions are a type of their own because `Provision of the Act` in uk-interpretation-application.l4 stops at section 21.
-- src:103 | (1) This Act applies to itself, to any Act passed after the commencement of this Act (subject , in the case of section 20(2A) to (6), to the provision made in section 20(2A) or (3) and, in the case of section 20A, to the provision made in that section) and, to the extent specified in Part I of Schedule 2, to Acts passed before the commencement of this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 22(1) (src:103), with s 20(2A) (src:88-89), s 20(3) (src:92) and s 20A (src:96-97)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision about references to EU instruments`
      day       IS A DATE
      `IP completion day` IS A DATE
      `the day section 20A came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Extent of application`
`section 22(1) with its carve-out — the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` provision day `IP completion day` `the day section 20A came into force` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` day)
    THEN `does not apply`
    ELSE CONSIDER provision
         WHEN `section 20(2A)` THEN IF day AT LEAST `IP completion day` THEN `applies without limit` ELSE `does not apply`
         WHEN `section 20(3)`  THEN IF day AT LEAST `IP completion day` THEN `applies without limit` ELSE `does not apply`
         WHEN `section 20(4)`  THEN IF day AT LEAST `IP completion day` THEN `applies without limit` ELSE `does not apply`
         WHEN `section 20(5)`  THEN IF day AT LEAST `IP completion day` THEN `applies without limit` ELSE `does not apply`
         WHEN `section 20(6)`  THEN IF day AT LEAST `IP completion day` THEN `applies without limit` ELSE `does not apply`
         WHEN `section 20A`    THEN IF day AT LEAST `the day section 20A came into force` THEN `applies without limit` ELSE `does not apply`
